IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wills-dates`
IMPORT `wills-claims`

-- Wills Act 1968 (ACT) -- worked cases for every exported question of wills-claims.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (and the readings in NOTES.md), not copied from the
-- encoding's output. Edges: 7 November 1991 and the day after; 6 and 7 October 1983; the 30th and 31st day after a
-- death; the last day of the 6 months and the day after; 6 months to a February with and without a 29th; the 4-month
-- window's last day and the day after; the 1-month and 7-day protections on the day before and the day they run out;
-- each formal requirement failing in turn; one and two witnesses.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the calendar date` d m y

`any day` MEANS `on` 1 1 2000

`undecided` MEANS `the Supreme Court has not yet decided`
`satisfied` MEANS `the Supreme Court is satisfied`
`not satisfied` MEANS `the Supreme Court is not satisfied`

`maker` MEANS `the will-maker`
`for maker` MEANS `another person, in the will-maker's presence and by the will-maker's direction`
`not for maker` MEANS `another person, but not in the will-maker's presence or not by the will-maker's direction`
`foot` MEANS `at the foot or end`
`apparent` MEANS `elsewhere, but placed so that it is apparent on the face of the document that it was meant to give effect to it (s 10)`
`not apparent` MEANS `elsewhere, and it is not apparent that it was meant to give effect to the document`

`no class` MEANS `none of these`
`soldier` MEANS `a member of the Defence Force in actual armed service`
`ACT only` MEANS `only the formal rules of the ACT Wills Act`
`where made` MEANS `the law of the place where the will was made`
`domicile` MEANS `the law of the place where the will-maker was domiciled when making it or at death`
`land` MEANS `the law of the place where the land it deals with is (for that land only)`

§§ `s 35 -- the 1991 provisions`

#ASSERT (NOT (`s 35 -- do the 1991 provisions apply to the will` (`on` 7 11 1991)))
#ASSERT `s 35 -- do the 1991 provisions apply to the will` (`on` 8 11 1991)
#ASSERT `s 35 -- do the 1991 provisions apply to the will` (`on` 1 3 2025)

§§ `s 8 -- a will made by a child`

#ASSERT `s 8 -- does my age stop the will being valid` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 8 is no bar: the will-maker was not a child when the will was made`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- does my age stop the will being valid` 17 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `valid as to age: the child was or had been married or in a civil union (s 8 (2))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- does my age stop the will being valid` 16 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `valid as to age: made in the terms of a Supreme Court order under s 8A (s 8 (4))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- does my age stop the will being valid` 17 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `valid as to age: made in contemplation of a marriage or civil union that has since taken place (s 8 (3))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- does my age stop the will being valid` 17 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet valid: made in contemplation of a marriage or civil union that has not taken place (s 8 (3))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- does my age stop the will being valid` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `valid as to age: a privileged will under s 16, which a child may make (s 8 (1), s 16 (7))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- does my age stop the will being valid` 17 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `valid as to age: a privileged will under s 16, which a child may make (s 8 (1), s 16 (7))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- does my age stop the will being valid` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not valid: a will made by a child (s 8 (1))`

§§ `s 8A, s 8B -- a child asking the court`

#ASSERT `s 8A, s 8B -- can I ask the court to let me make or revoke my will` 18 FALSE `make a will` FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `you are not a child: you need no order`
#ASSERT `s 8A, s 8B -- can I ask the court to let me make or revoke my will` 16 TRUE `make a will` FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `you need no order: a child who is or has been married or in a civil union may make or revoke a will (s 8 (2))`
#ASSERT `s 8A, s 8B -- can I ask the court to let me make or revoke my will` 16 FALSE `revoke my will or part of it` FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `s 8B is not open to you: you have no valid will to revoke`
#ASSERT `s 8A, s 8B -- can I ask the court to let me make or revoke my will` 16 FALSE `make a will` FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `you may apply; the Supreme Court may make the order only if satisfied that you understand it, it reflects your intentions and it is reasonable (s 8A (2), s 8B (2))`
#ASSERT `s 8A, s 8B -- can I ask the court to let me make or revoke my will` 16 FALSE `make a will` FALSE `satisfied` EQUALS `the Supreme Court may make the order: it is satisfied of the s 8A (2) or s 8B (2) matters`
#ASSERT `s 8A, s 8B -- can I ask the court to let me make or revoke my will` 17 FALSE `revoke my will or part of it` TRUE `not satisfied` EQUALS `the Supreme Court cannot make the order: it is not satisfied of the s 8A (2) or s 8B (2) matters`
#ASSERT `s 8A, s 8B -- can I ask the court to let me make or revoke my will` 17 FALSE `revoke my will or part of it` TRUE `satisfied` EQUALS `the Supreme Court may make the order: it is satisfied of the s 8A (2) or s 8B (2) matters`

§§ `s 9, s 10 -- signing and witnessing`

#ASSERT `s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `maker` `foot` 2 2
#ASSERT `s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `maker` `foot` 3 2
#ASSERT `s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `for maker` `foot` 2 2
#ASSERT `s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `maker` `apparent` 2 2
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `maker` `not apparent` 2 2))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `not for maker` `foot` 2 2))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `nobody` `foot` 2 2))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` FALSE `maker` `foot` 2 2))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `maker` `foot` 2 1))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 9 -- was the will signed and witnessed as required` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 2))

§§ `Is the will valid as to form`

-- A home-made will with one witness, the will-maker died 1 March 2025, unless varied.
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 2 2 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `ACT only` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `undecided` EQUALS `valid: signed and witnessed as s 9 requires`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `ACT only` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `undecided` EQUALS `not valid as made; it is a will only if the Supreme Court is satisfied the deceased intended it to be (s 11A)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `ACT only` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `satisfied` EQUALS `a will: the Supreme Court is satisfied the deceased intended the document to be their will (s 11A)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `ACT only` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `not satisfied` EQUALS `not a will: the Supreme Court is not satisfied the deceased intended it to be their will (s 11A)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `ACT only` FALSE `any day` `undecided` EQUALS `not valid as made, and s 11A is only for a document of a person who has died`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` FALSE `nobody` `foot` 0 0 `soldier` FALSE FALSE FALSE `ACT only` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `undecided` EQUALS `valid: a privileged will of a person on active service or in a like class (s 16)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` TRUE FALSE FALSE `ACT only` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `undecided` EQUALS `valid: an international will under the convention (s 16K, schedule 1)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `nobody` `foot` 0 0 `no class` FALSE TRUE FALSE `ACT only` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `undecided` EQUALS `valid: a will made under a Supreme Court order, in writing, signed by the registrar and sealed (s 16F)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `nobody` `foot` 0 0 `no class` FALSE FALSE TRUE `ACT only` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `undecided` EQUALS `valid: a statutory will made under the law of the place where the person lived (s 16I)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `where made` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `undecided` EQUALS `valid: properly made under the law of a place connected with the will-maker (Part 2A, s 15C, s 15D)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `domicile` FALSE `any day` `undecided` EQUALS `valid: properly made under the law of a place connected with the will-maker (Part 2A, s 15C, s 15D)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `where made` TRUE (`on` 7 10 1983) `undecided` EQUALS `valid: properly made under the law of a place connected with the will-maker (Part 2A, s 15C, s 15D)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `where made` TRUE (`on` 6 10 1983) `undecided` EQUALS `not valid as made; it is a will only if the Supreme Court is satisfied the deceased intended it to be (s 11A)`
#ASSERT `is the will valid as to form` TRUE `maker` `foot` 1 1 `no class` FALSE FALSE FALSE `land` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) `undecided` EQUALS `valid so far as it deals with land in the place whose law it followed (s 15D (1) (b))`

§§ `s 12 -- alterations`

`margin` MEANS `in the margin, or elsewhere on the will, opposite or near the alteration`
`memo` MEANS `at the foot or end of, or opposite, a memorandum in the will that refers to the alteration`
`elsewhere` MEANS `somewhere else on the will`
`unsigned` MEANS `the alteration was not signed`

#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` FALSE `nobody` `unsigned` 0 0 TRUE TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `s 12 does not apply: the alteration was made before the will was executed`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` TRUE `maker` `margin` 2 2 TRUE TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `the alteration counts: it was signed and witnessed as s 12 requires`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` TRUE `for maker` `memo` 2 2 FALSE FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `the alteration counts: it was signed and witnessed as s 12 requires`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` TRUE `maker` `elsewhere` 2 2 TRUE TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `whether it counts is not settled by s 12: the signatures are not where s 12 (2) deems them to comply`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` TRUE `maker` `margin` 2 1 TRUE TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `the alteration does not count unless the Supreme Court is satisfied the deceased intended it (s 11A); the will is read as before`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` TRUE `maker` `margin` 1 1 TRUE TRUE `satisfied` EQUALS `the alteration counts: the Supreme Court is satisfied the deceased intended it (s 11A)`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` TRUE `nobody` `unsigned` 0 0 TRUE TRUE `not satisfied` EQUALS `the alteration does not count: the will is read as it was before`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` TRUE `nobody` `unsigned` 0 0 TRUE FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `the alteration does not count: the will is read as it was before`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` TRUE `nobody` `unsigned` 0 0 FALSE FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `the alteration does not count, but the will is read without the original words, which cannot be made out (s 12 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- does the change to the will count` TRUE `nobody` `unsigned` 0 0 FALSE TRUE `not satisfied` EQUALS `the alteration does not count, but the will is read without the original words, which cannot be made out (s 12 (1))`

§§ `s 12A -- rectification`

-- 6 months commencing 10 January 2025 end on 9 July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 12A -- the last day to apply for rectification without leave` (`on` 10 1 2025) EQUALS `on` 9 7 2025
-- 31 August 2025: no 31 February 2026, so the period ends with February.
#ASSERT `s 12A -- the last day to apply for rectification without leave` (`on` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 12A -- the last day to apply for rectification without leave` (`on` 30 8 2027) EQUALS `on` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `s 12A -- the last day to apply for rectification without leave` (`on` 29 8 2027) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2028
#ASSERT `s 12A -- the last day to apply for rectification without leave` (`on` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `on` 31 8 2025
#ASSERT `s 12A -- the last day to apply for rectification without leave` (`on` 15 10 2025) EQUALS `on` 14 4 2026

`probate` MEANS `on` 10 1 2025
`no leave` MEANS `leave not sought or not yet decided`

#ASSERT `s 12A -- can I apply for rectification` `probate` TRUE (`on` 9 7 2025) (`on` 1 8 2025) `no leave` EQUALS `in time: you applied on or before the last day`
#ASSERT `s 12A -- can I apply for rectification` `probate` TRUE (`on` 10 7 2025) (`on` 1 8 2025) `no leave` EQUALS `out of time: you may apply only with the Supreme Court's leave (s 12A (3))`
#ASSERT `s 12A -- can I apply for rectification` `probate` TRUE (`on` 10 7 2025) (`on` 1 8 2025) `the Supreme Court has given leave` EQUALS `out of time, but the Supreme Court has given leave: you may apply`
#ASSERT `s 12A -- can I apply for rectification` `probate` TRUE (`on` 10 7 2025) (`on` 1 8 2025) `the Supreme Court has refused leave` EQUALS `out of time, and the Supreme Court has refused leave`
#ASSERT `s 12A -- can I apply for rectification` `probate` FALSE `any day` (`on` 9 7 2025) `no leave` EQUALS `still in time: apply on or before the last day`
#ASSERT `s 12A -- can I apply for rectification` `probate` FALSE `any day` (`on` 10 7 2025) `no leave` EQUALS `out of time: you may apply only with the Supreme Court's leave (s 12A (3))`
#ASSERT `s 12A -- can I apply for rectification` `probate` TRUE (`on` 10 1 2025) (`on` 1 8 2025) `no leave` EQUALS `in time: you applied on or before the last day`
#ASSERT `s 12A -- can I apply for rectification` `probate` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2025) (`on` 1 8 2025) `no leave` EQUALS `in time: you applied on or before the last day`

-- s 12A (4): the 4 months commencing 10 January 2025 end on 9 May 2025.
#ASSERT `s 12A (4) -- the day the notice asks me to apply by` `probate` (`on` 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (`on` 31 3 2025)
#ASSERT `s 12A (4) -- the day the notice asks me to apply by` `probate` (`on` 9 5 2025) EQUALS JUST (`on` 8 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 12A (4) -- the day the notice asks me to apply by` `probate` (`on` 31 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (`on` 28 2 2025)
#ASSERT `s 12A (4) -- the day the notice asks me to apply by` `probate` (`on` 10 1 2025) EQUALS JUST (`on` 9 2 2025)
#ASSERT `s 12A (4) -- the day the notice asks me to apply by` `probate` (`on` 10 5 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12A (4) -- the day the notice asks me to apply by` `probate` (`on` 9 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 12A (5): notice published 1 March 2025; the month since it has elapsed from 2 April 2025 (fork F2). The 6 months
-- expired at the end of 9 July 2025. Leave given 1 August 2025: 7 days have elapsed from 9 August 2025.
`protected a` MEANS `protected (s 12A (5) (a)): a month had passed since the notice and no application was known of; you may still recover the property from those who received it (s 12A (6))`
`protected b i` MEANS `protected (s 12A (5) (b) (i)): the 6 months had expired and no application or leave was known of; you may still recover the property from those who received it (s 12A (6))`
`protected b ii` MEANS `protected (s 12A (5) (b) (ii)): 7 days had passed since leave was given without an application; you may still recover the property from those who received it (s 12A (6))`
`unprotected` MEANS `s 12A (5) gives the personal representative no protection on these facts; whether they are liable is for the general law, and you may also recover the property from those who received it (s 12A (6))`

#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) (`on` 2 4 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `protected a`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) (`on` 1 4 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) (`on` 2 4 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2025) (`on` 2 4 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `protected a`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` TRUE (`on` 10 5 2025) (`on` 1 7 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` FALSE `any day` (`on` 10 7 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `protected b i`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` FALSE `any day` (`on` 9 7 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` FALSE `any day` (`on` 10 7 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` FALSE `any day` (`on` 10 7 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` FALSE `any day` (`on` 9 8 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS `protected b ii`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` FALSE `any day` (`on` 8 8 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS `unprotected`
#ASSERT `s 12A (5) -- is the personal representative protected` `probate` FALSE `any day` (`on` 9 8 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS `unprotected`

§§ `s 12B -- evidence`

`to construe` MEANS `to work out what the will means`
`to show circumstances` MEANS `to show the surrounding circumstances that make the will ambiguous or uncertain`

#ASSERT `s 12B -- can the evidence be used` `meaningless` `to construe` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12B -- can the evidence be used` `ambiguous or uncertain on its face` `to construe` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12B -- can the evidence be used` `ambiguous or uncertain in the light of the surrounding circumstances` `to construe` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12B -- can the evidence be used` `clear` `to construe` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12B -- can the evidence be used` `ambiguous or uncertain in the light of the surrounding circumstances` `to show circumstances` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12B -- can the evidence be used` `clear` `to show circumstances` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 3A -- a will for a person without capacity`

#ASSERT `Part 3A -- can the court make a will for someone without capacity` FALSE TRUE `satisfied` EQUALS `no: the person has died, and the court must not make the order (s 16A (3))`
#ASSERT `Part 3A -- can the court make a will for someone without capacity` TRUE FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `not under Part 3A: it is for a person who does not have testamentary capacity`
#ASSERT `Part 3A -- can the court make a will for someone without capacity` TRUE TRUE `undecided` EQUALS `apply first for the Supreme Court's leave, with the s 16B information; leave must be refused unless the court is satisfied of the s 16E matters`
#ASSERT `Part 3A -- can the court make a will for someone without capacity` TRUE TRUE `satisfied` EQUALS `the Supreme Court may give leave and make the order (s 16C); the will must be in writing, signed by the registrar and sealed while the person is alive (s 16F)`
#ASSERT `Part 3A -- can the court make a will for someone without capacity` TRUE TRUE `not satisfied` EQUALS `leave must be refused: the Supreme Court is not satisfied of the s 16E matters`

§§ `s 20 -- marriage after the will`

#ASSERT `s 20 -- did the marriage revoke the will` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 20 does not arise: no marriage, civil union or civil partnership after the will was made`
#ASSERT `s 20 -- did the marriage revoke the will` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not revoked: the will was expressed to be made in contemplation of that marriage, civil union or civil partnership (s 20 (1))`
#ASSERT `s 20 -- did the marriage revoke the will` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not revoked: the gift to the person married stands, and so does the rest of the will (s 20 (3))`
#ASSERT `s 20 -- did the marriage revoke the will` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the gift to the person married stands, but the rest of the will is revoked: a contrary intention appears (s 20 (3) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 20 -- did the marriage revoke the will` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `revoked, except so far as it exercises a power of appointment over property that would not pass to an executor or administrator in default (s 20 (2))`
#ASSERT `s 20 -- did the marriage revoke the will` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `revoked by the marriage, civil union or civil partnership (s 20 (1))`

§§ `s 20A -- divorce after the will`

`divorce` MEANS `divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cwlth)`
`gift` MEANS `a gift, or a power of appointment`
`executor` MEANS `an appointment as executor, trustee or guardian`
`debt` MEANS `a charge or direction to pay a debt owed to them`

#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `separation only, or it has not ended in any of those ways` TRUE `gift` FALSE `not satisfied` EQUALS `s 20A does not apply: the relationship has not been terminated in a way s 20A (4) describes`
#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `divorce` FALSE `gift` FALSE `not satisfied` EQUALS `s 20A does not apply: the relationship ended before the will was made`
#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `divorce` TRUE `debt` FALSE `not satisfied` EQUALS `not affected: a provision to pay a debt owed to the former partner stands (s 20A (1) (a), (3) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `divorce` TRUE `gift` TRUE `not satisfied` EQUALS `not revoked: the will was republished after the termination without showing an intention to revoke (s 20A (2) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `divorce` TRUE `gift` FALSE `satisfied` EQUALS `not revoked: the Supreme Court is satisfied the will-maker did not intend to revoke it (s 20A (2) (a))`
#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `divorce` TRUE `gift` FALSE `undecided` EQUALS `revoked unless the Supreme Court is satisfied the will-maker did not intend to revoke it (s 20A (1), (2) (a))`
#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `divorce` TRUE `gift` FALSE `not satisfied` EQUALS `revoked: the property passes as if the former partner had died before the will-maker (s 20A (1) (a), (c))`
#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `divorce` TRUE `executor` FALSE `not satisfied` EQUALS `omitted: the will is read as if the former partner had not been appointed (s 20A (1) (b))`
#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `a civil partnership ended under the Domestic Relationships Act 1994, division 4A.4, other than by death` TRUE `gift` FALSE `not satisfied` EQUALS `revoked: the property passes as if the former partner had died before the will-maker (s 20A (1) (a), (c))`
#ASSERT `s 20A -- what the divorce did to the provision for the former partner` `a decree of nullity under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cwlth)` TRUE `executor` FALSE `not satisfied` EQUALS `omitted: the will is read as if the former partner had not been appointed (s 20A (1) (b))`

§§ `s 21, s 22 -- revocation and revival`

#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE FALSE `it was not destroyed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not revoked (s 21)`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` TRUE FALSE `it was not destroyed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `revoked by a later valid will (s 21 (b) (i))`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE TRUE `it was not destroyed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `revoked by a document executed like a will showing the intention to revoke (s 21 (b) (ii))`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE FALSE `the will-maker destroyed it, meaning to revoke it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `revoked by being destroyed with the intention of revoking it (s 21 (b) (iii))`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE FALSE `someone else destroyed it in the will-maker's presence and at their direction, the will-maker meaning to revoke it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `revoked by being destroyed with the intention of revoking it (s 21 (b) (iii))`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE FALSE `someone else destroyed it, but not in the will-maker's presence or not at their direction` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not revoked (s 21)`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE FALSE `it was destroyed without any intention of revoking it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not revoked (s 21)`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE FALSE `it was not destroyed` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `revoked by a privileged declaration of a person on active service or in a like class (s 21 (a), s 16)`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE FALSE `it was not destroyed` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `revoked by a later marriage, civil union or civil partnership (s 20)`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE FALSE `it was not destroyed` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `revoked under a Supreme Court order (s 8B, s 16A)`
#ASSERT `s 21 -- has the will been revoked` FALSE FALSE `it was not destroyed` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `revoked: the Supreme Court is satisfied the deceased intended a document to revoke it (s 11A)`

#ASSERT `s 22 -- has the revoked will been revived` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22 -- has the revoked will been revived` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 22 -- has the revoked will been revived` FALSE FALSE))

§§ `s 31C -- surviving by 30 days`

-- The deceased died 1 March 2025. The 30 days after are 2 to 31 March 2025 (fork F3).
`death` MEANS `on` 1 3 2025
`survived` MEANS `does not lapse under s 31C: the beneficiary survived the deceased by 30 days`
`lapses` MEANS `lapses: the beneficiary is taken to have died before the deceased (s 31C (2))`

#ASSERT `s 31C -- does the gift lapse for not surviving by 30 days` `death` TRUE (`on` 1 4 2025) `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `survived`
#ASSERT `s 31C -- does the gift lapse for not surviving by 30 days` `death` TRUE (`on` 31 3 2025) `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `lapses`
#ASSERT `s 31C -- does the gift lapse for not surviving by 30 days` `death` TRUE (`on` 28 2 2025) `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `lapses`
#ASSERT `s 31C -- does the gift lapse for not surviving by 30 days` `death` FALSE `any day` (`on` 31 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet known: the 30 days after the death have not ended`
#ASSERT `s 31C -- does the gift lapse for not surviving by 30 days` `death` FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 4 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `survived`
#ASSERT `s 31C -- does the gift lapse for not surviving by 30 days` `death` TRUE (`on` 31 3 2025) `any day` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `does not lapse: a contrary intention appears from the will or from evidence under s 12B (s 31C (2))`
#ASSERT `s 31C -- does the gift lapse for not surviving by 30 days` `death` TRUE (`on` 31 3 2025) `any day` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `does not lapse: otherwise the estate would pass to the Territory (s 31C (3))`
-- Across February in a leap year: died 31 January 2024; the 30th day after is 1 March 2024.
#ASSERT `s 31C -- does the gift lapse for not surviving by 30 days` (`on` 31 1 2024) TRUE (`on` 1 3 2024) `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `lapses`
#ASSERT `s 31C -- does the gift lapse for not surviving by 30 days` (`on` 31 1 2024) TRUE (`on` 2 3 2024) `any day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `survived`

§§ `s 31 -- my parent's gift`

`child` MEANS `a child who survived the will-maker by 30 days`
`grandchild` MEANS `a grandchild who survived the will-maker by 30 days, whose parent did not`

#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `child` 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `child` 2 1 0 EQUALS JUST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `grandchild` 2 1 2 EQUALS JUST (1 DIVIDED BY 6)
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `grandchild` 1 1 1 EQUALS JUST (1 DIVIDED BY 2)
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `child` 1 0 0 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `child` 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `child` 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `child` 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `child` 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `child` 3 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `I did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `I did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` 2 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 31 -- my share of my parent's gift` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `a more remote descendant` 1 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 31B -- a gift to the will-maker's issue`

#ASSERT `s 31B -- my share of a gift to the will-maker's issue` FALSE `child` 4 0 0 EQUALS JUST (1 DIVIDED BY 4)
#ASSERT `s 31B -- my share of a gift to the will-maker's issue` FALSE `grandchild` 2 1 3 EQUALS JUST (1 DIVIDED BY 9)
#ASSERT `s 31B -- my share of a gift to the will-maker's issue` FALSE `child` 1 0 0 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 31B -- my share of a gift to the will-maker's issue` TRUE `child` 4 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31B -- my share of a gift to the will-maker's issue` FALSE `a more remote descendant` 2 1 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31B -- my share of a gift to the will-maker's issue` FALSE `I did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` 2 1 0 EQUALS JUST 0
